// The Trollheim summit and the God Wars valley, grafted from the OSRS map by
// tools/models/graftosrsmap.py (--levels 0 --box 2893,3702,2932,3759).
//
// Why the map had to come from a newer cache: the 377 square has no God Wars approach at all. The
// dungeon opened in August 2007, a year after this revision, and the valley it sits in was carved
// into Trollheim then. Our m45_58 had the whole of it as solid rock - 2898,3716, where the boulder
// belongs, was a single isolated walkable tile with nothing adjoining it, which is why no climbing
// rock could ever have led there. 474 is no better: its terrain stops at the same z=3695 as ours,
// and this cache has no XTEA key for l45_57 or l45_58, so its locs cannot be read at all.
//
// The graft is the 813 tiles of ground OSRS has here and we did not, meeting our mountain at the
// north-east shoulder (2899..2902, 3701..3702). Nothing functional was displaced: all 22 kinds of
// 377 loc inside the box are scenery - snow, dug-up soil, ice chunks, mountain rocks - with no
// right-click option on any of them and not one reference from any script.
//
// osrsloc_26415 and osrsloc_26382 below are the Boulder and the Little crack, which this tree
// already carries as gwd_boulder and gwd_crack in gwd_entrance.loc with the ops and the scripts on
// them. The two map placements were repointed to those, so the pair here is unused. They are left
// defined rather than deleted because loc.pack numbers by position: dropping them would renumber
// every loc the graft appended after them, and the .jm2 files already name those ids.

// OSRS locs grafted by tools/models/graftosrsmap.py (osrslocimport.py).
// Models re-encoded by osrs2ob2.py with the loc recolours baked in.

